 "answer_text": "Found 11 disease records and 2 gene records for BRCA1 and BRCA2 [2][3][4][5][8][9][10][11][12][13][14][15][16]. \n\nGermline mutations in BRCA1 account for roughly 40% of inherited breast cancers and over 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers [1]. \n\nBRCA1-Associated Diseases\n\nBRCA1 is linked to familial cancer of breast [2], familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 [3], pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 [4], and Fanconi anemia complementation group S [5]. Preneoplastic stromal cells have been shown to promote BRCA1-mediated breast tumorigenesis [6]. BRCA1 also functions as an endocrine and metabolic regulator [7]. \n\nBRCA2 is associated with medulloblastoma [8], Fanconi anemia complementation group D1 [9], familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 2 [10], glioma susceptibility 3 [11], familial prostate cancer [12], pancreatic cancer susceptibility 2 [13], and Wilms tumor 1 [14]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:672, name: BRCA1 DNA repair associated [15]. Gene NCBIGene:675, name: BRCA2 DNA repair associated [16]. Gene symbol: BRCA1 [17]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Familial cancer of breast [2]. Disease name: Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 [3]. Disease name: Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 [4]. Disease name: Fanconi anemia complementation group S [5]. Disease name: Medulloblastoma [8]. Disease name: Fanconi anemia complementation group D1 [9]. Disease name: Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 2 [10]. Disease name: Glioma susceptibility 3 [11]. Disease name: Familial prostate cancer [12]. Disease name: Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 2 [13]. Disease name: Wilms tumor 1 [14]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: BRCA1-BARD1 promotes RAD51-mediated homologous DNA pairing [18]. Pubmed title: BRCA1: An Endocrine and Metabolic Regulator [7]. Pubmed title: Preneoplastic stromal cells promote BRCA1-mediated breast tumorigenesis [6]. Pubmed title: Mechanism of BRCA1-BARD1 functi